# Upstream baseline for the mainline H5000M build.
#
# WHY openwrt/openwrt main (SNAPSHOT) AND NOT 25.12
# -------------------------------------------------
# Hiveton H5000M support was added upstream by
#   6487cc9a1f  "mediatek: add support for Hiveton H5000M"   (2026-01-09)
# and that commit is only on `main`.  Verified against the published images:
#
#   releases/25.12.0 .. 25.12.5 -> profiles.json contains NO hiveton_h5000m
#   snapshots/                  -> profiles.json contains hiveton_h5000m
#
# The openwrt-25.12 *branch* head does carry the device (cherry-picked after
# the 25.12.5 tag), but no released 25.12.x image does, so SNAPSHOT `main` is
# simultaneously the newest and the only mainline upstream that ships H5000M
# firmware today.  It is also what every in-tree plugin for this board is
# verified against (luci-app-h5000m-fancontrol: "OpenWrt SNAPSHOT";
# ddimension feed: `stable/snapshot/aarch64_cortex-a53`).
#
# Set OPENWRT_REPO_BRANCH=openwrt-25.12 to build the 25.12 branch instead once
# 25.12.6 ships the device.
OPENWRT_REPO_URL=https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt.git
OPENWRT_REPO_BRANCH=main

# Last revision this harness was validated against: a full firmware build
# succeeded on it.  Used when OPENWRT_TRACK=pinned, and recorded as the
# fallback baseline in BUILD-INFO.txt when tracking `latest`.
#
# ★ READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING THE VALUE.  Three earlier notes here were wrong
#   and their errors cost about twenty CI runs.  Here is the corrected
#   account, with the evidence for each claim.  The short version: this pin
#   alone never made the build reproducible, because the FEEDS were never
#   pinned.  See FEEDS_SNAPSHOT_DATE in this file and pin_all_feeds() in
#   scripts/local-build.sh.  Change the two together.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY BREAKS (measured, and it is not what the earlier notes said)
#
#   Same tree, same upstream pin (bfb98589), 19 hours apart:
#
#     2026-09-29T12:40Z feeds  -> 0 dangling refs,  26 recursive deps, BUILD OK
#     2026-09-30T07:14Z feeds  -> 8 dangling refs, 176 recursive deps, qmodem DROPPED
#
#   The only input that moved between those two runs is feed content.  The
#   feed delta is traceable to the minute - openwrt/packages committed
#   be93cc55 (`libdrm: depend on video-support`) and 6e7270bc (`libevdev:
#   depend on input-support`) at 2026-09-29T14:50Z, 2h10m after the green
#   build.  Those symbols live in upstream's new `Hardware support` category,
#   which a tree pinned at bfb98589 (09-29T08:49) does not have, so the feed
#   ends up depending on packages that do not exist:
#
#     WARNING: No feed for package 'audio-support' found
#     WARNING: Makefile 'package/feeds/packages/libdrm/Makefile' has a
#              dependency on 'video-support', which does not exist
#
#   From there the Kconfig graph is perturbed enough that the QModem closure
#   is silently dropped and verify_config() refuses to ship - correctly.
#
#   In the green run the missing-package list has five entries (babeld,
#   kmod-mhi-wwan, kmod-qca-nss-drv, quectel-CM-5G, quectel-cm) and none of
#   them is a *-support symbol; in the failing run it has ten, the five extra
#   being audio-support, video-support, input-support, scanner-support and
#   dvb-support.
#
# WHAT THIS PIN IS NOT
#
#   It is NOT the fix, and pinning it more precisely will not make the build
#   green.  bfb98589 is kept only because it is the revision the one green
#   build happened to run on, which makes it the correct half of the
#   reproduction; the other half is FEEDS_SNAPSHOT_DATE, set to the same
#   moment.
#
# ★ TWO THEORIES THAT WERE TESTED AND DISPROVED - DO NOT RE-DERIVE THEM
#
#   1. "Upstream 6e638524 reordered scripts/package-metadata.pl's category
#      walk and that is what drops QModem."  Disproved by pinning the tree to
#      bfb98589, which predates that commit by four commits, and still losing
#      qmodem (`36682079340`).  Identical upstream, opposite outcome - the
#      cause is not in the tree.  The reorder is real and may well contribute
#      to how the cycles resolve, but it is not the trigger.
#
#   2. "The wwand feed is what keeps qmodem alive."  It was based on three
#      runs in which `wwand present` correlated with `qmodem survived`.  The
#      fourth run refuted it: feed restored, its packages installed, qmodem
#      still dropped.  Two data points agreeing is not a mechanism.
#
#   Recursive-dependency counts across the runs were 26 / 14 / 156 / 166 /
#   176 / 178 and never predicted the outcome.  Do not tune feed lists or
#   feeds.conf to move that number; it is a symptom.
#
# WHAT TO DO WHEN ADVANCING
#
#   Bump OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION and FEEDS_SNAPSHOT_DATE to the SAME moment,
#   run a workflow_dispatch with pinned=true, and require a complete firmware
#   - `Verified all emitted packages survived defconfig` on the way, and real
#   artefacts at the end.  To follow main instead of pinning, drop both knobs
#   together (OPENWRT_TRACK=latest and an empty FEEDS_SNAPSHOT_DATE); half of
#   that pair is exactly the inconsistency described above.
OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION=bfb985894411647c61d48f92946c6b2fc775f83a
OPENWRT_PINNED_SNAPSHOT=r0-bfb9858

# The other half of the reproduction.  Every feed in feeds.conf.default names
# a branch, so without this the feeds track master/main and the build is a
# function of the calendar.  The value is read as `git rev-list -1 --before=`
# - it is a MOMENT, not a commit - and every feed is checked out at its last
# commit at or before it.  Must name the same moment as the pin above.
#
# 2026-09-29T12:40Z is the moment the one green build checked its feeds out.
# Advancing it is a deliberate act: move both knobs, then rebuild.
FEEDS_SNAPSHOT_DATE=2026-09-29T12:40:00Z

# ★ FEEDS_FOLLOW_TREE — derive the cutoff above from the tree itself, instead of
#   hand-maintaining a second number that has to match it.
#
#   The rule "both knobs must name the SAME moment" lived only in the comment
#   above, and nothing enforced it.  Monday's cron runs with OPENWRT_TRACK=latest
#   and no `pinned` input, so the tree moves every week while this file does not:
#   the scheduled build compiles this week's tree against feeds frozen at
#   2026-09-29, and the apk repository it publishes therefore serves packages
#   from 2026-09-29 for as long as nobody edits this file.  That is not a wrong
#   value, it is two inputs where there should be one.
#
#   With FEEDS_FOLLOW_TREE=true, pin_all_feeds() reads the upstream checkout's
#   own commit time and rolls the feeds back to that instant.  "Tree and feeds
#   from the same moment" then holds by construction in BOTH modes - a `latest`
#   tree gets the feeds from the week it was fetched, a `pinned` tree gets the
#   feeds from its pin - so the scheduled build tracks upstream without anyone
#   bumping a date, and there is no combination in which the feeds are ahead of
#   the tree (the dangling-reference case) or behind it (the frozen case).
#
#   When on, FEEDS_SNAPSHOT_DATE above is IGNORED, not merged.
#
#   Default false on purpose: it changes what every scheduled build compiles and
#   no run has exercised it yet.  It gets turned on by a green workflow_dispatch
#   with it enabled - the same way the feed pin itself was - and not by the
#   commit that introduces it.
FEEDS_FOLLOW_TREE=false



# `latest` (default) follows the branch head on every build — that is the point
# of a scheduled auto-build.  `pinned` builds OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION so a build
# can be reproduced exactly; scripts/local-build.sh --pinned selects it.
OPENWRT_TRACK=latest

# Target triple, as published by OpenWrt.
OPENWRT_TARGET=mediatek
OPENWRT_SUBTARGET=filogic
OPENWRT_PROFILE=hiveton_h5000m
OPENWRT_ARCH=aarch64_cortex-a53
OPENWRT_IMAGE_PREFIX=openwrt-mediatek-filogic-hiveton_h5000m

# The ddimension WWAN dialer feed.  write_feeds_conf() appends it *only* when
# ENABLE_WWAND=true.  It must not be installed on a QModem or mt5700m build:
# the feed carries libubus-lua-async, whose PROVIDES:=libubus-lua plus
# CONFLICTS:=libubus-lua pair becomes a Kconfig loop against the base
# libubus-lua and makes defconfig drop the entire qmodem dependency chain.
# feeds.conf.default has the full chain; verify_config() refuses to ship
# firmware when it happens, which is how it was caught.
#
# Before this was conditional the feed was unconditional in
# feeds.conf.default, so every QModem build since the feed gained that
# package failed its package check.  The H5000M has no wwand user today:
# the units in the wild carry a Quectel RG520N-CN and run QModem.
WWAND_REPO_URL=https://github.com/ddimension/openwrt-repo.git
WWAND_REPO_BRANCH=main

# Optional fallback modem stack.  luci-app-mt5700m (the FAN789 panel for the
# built-in MT5700M) hard-depends on `ubus-at-daemon` and `sms-tool_q`, and both
# are packaged only by the QModem feed.  write_feeds_conf() therefore appends
# this feed *only* when ENABLE_MT5700M=true; a wwand build never sees it, since
# the two stacks are mutually exclusive and QModem brings its own drivers.
#
# A SHA CANNOT GO HERE.  This line was briefly the full commit id c49654ef...
# and it broke the build at `feeds update` before defconfig ever ran:
#
#   Updating feed 'qmodem' from '...;c49654efc870f53712ee8e25bf181722eb1466d9'
#   fatal: Remote branch c49654efc870f53712ee8e25bf181722eb1466d9 not found
#
# scripts/feeds does `git clone --branch <ref>`, and --branch takes a branch or
# a tag NAME, not a raw object id.  The name stays `main`; pinning by commit is
# done after the feed is checked out instead - see pin_qmodem_feed() in
# scripts/local-build.sh, which fetches the SHA and checks it out in place.
QMODEM_REPO_URL=https://github.com/FUjr/QModem.git
QMODEM_REPO_BRANCH=main

# The commit pin_qmodem_feed() checks the checkout out at, or empty to follow
# the branch head.  The green build of 09-29 used c49654ef (09-19T19:28, "luci:
# restore standard qmodem-next packaging"), so that is the reproducible
# baseline.  Set this empty to let the feed float again.
QMODEM_PINNED_REVISION=c49654efc870f53712ee8e25bf181722eb1466d9
